WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:12.300
And that is our plan.

2
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.466
It will not be easy.

3
00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:16.633
Be very cautious.

4
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:20.833
We, as the Ninja Corps, profess our eternal loyalty.

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.866
Glory to you, Kagetomo.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.100
Glory to Kagetomo.

7
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.300
Just you wait, Hanzo.

8
00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:38.566
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

9
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:42.300
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

10
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.233
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

11
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.500
♪ Pokémon ♪

12
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.433
♪ Pokémon ♪

13
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.666
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

14
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:53.933
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

15
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.200
♪ Pokémon ♪

16
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:57.100
♪ Pokémon ♪

17
00:00:57.166 --> 00:00:58.400
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

18
00:01:11.366 --> 00:01:13.433
- Great, Frogadier.
- Pika!

19
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.566
- They said lunch is ready now.
- Froga.

20
00:01:17.366 --> 00:01:21.000
Ash may be on a quest to win his eighth Kalos Gym badge,

21
00:01:21.066 --> 00:01:24.033
but for now, our heroes are taking a lunch break.

22
00:01:30.466 --> 00:01:32.833
- Froga.
- Something wrong, Frogadier?

23
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.466
Frogadier!

24
00:01:38.666 --> 00:01:39.766
Wow, well done.

25
00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.800
It's Sanpei. And Greninja.

26
00:01:42.866 --> 00:01:46.300
When we saw you here, we thought we'd sneak up on you.

27
00:01:46.366 --> 00:01:48.533
But I didn't think you'd notice us first.

28
00:01:48.866 --> 00:01:51.933
- You're improving, Frogadier.
- Frog.

29
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.466
It's been a while. It's great to see you.

30
00:01:54.766 --> 00:01:55.966
And you, too.

31
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.833
Perfect. We just finished making lunch.

32
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.733
Why don't you have lunch with us?

33
00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.333
Uh, thank you.

34
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.100
Ninja Village?

35
00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:13.300
That's right. You see, Greninja and I are on our way back home,

36
00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.200
so that we can be a part of tomorrow's village festival.

37
00:02:16.266 --> 00:02:17.300
What's it like?

38
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:19.933
Are there lots of ninja in Ninja Village?

39
00:02:20.233 --> 00:02:23.366
Sure. The place is filled with ninja villagers and Pokémon,

40
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:25.733
who are busy training hard every single day.

41
00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:29.733
Hmm. Ah! So, are there any girl ninja?

42
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:31.966
Of course. They're pretty, too.

43
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.233
Wow, I really wanna go.

44
00:02:34.633 --> 00:02:35.766
It sounds great.

45
00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:37.200
I'd like to see it, as well.

46
00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:40.166
- I'll bet it's an awesome time.
- Pika!

47
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.300
Well, we would be happy to invite all of you.

48
00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:45.400
- Right, Greninja?
- Gren.

49
00:02:45.966 --> 00:02:49.366
Now that we've settled that, time to have some fun.

50
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.066
Ninja Bonnie.

51
00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:09.866
What's wrong?

52
00:03:11.766 --> 00:03:12.600
Mountain.

53
00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:13.866
River.

54
00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:20.466
Sanpei. Welcome home.

55
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.533
Ha!

56
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.366
It's great to be back.

57
00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:25.233
So, are they your friends?

58
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:27.133
- Yes.
- Go see everyone.

59
00:03:27.366 --> 00:03:29.100
- They'll be glad you're back.
- Right.

60
00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:33.766
It's inside a cave?

61
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.233
It's pitch-black.

62
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.066
You'll be amazed when you see it.

63
00:03:41.066 --> 00:03:42.000
Awesome.

64
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.633
Welcome to Ninja Village.

65
00:03:49.566 --> 00:03:51.800
- And up we go.
- Everybody.

66
00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:53.633
I'm back.

67
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.633
Greninja.

68
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.100
Sanpei? Hey, it's Sanpei!

69
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.766
Ippei, Nihei. Sanpei's back.

70
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.600
Sanpei, it's good to have you home, brother.

71
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.400
It makes me very happy to see both my brothers doing so well.

72
00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:15.000
So, Frogadier evolved into a Greninja.

73
00:04:15.066 --> 00:04:17.399
- It's gotten really strong.
- Gren.

74
00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:19.333
And who are they, Sanpei?

75
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.833
I'd like you both to meet my friends.

76
00:04:21.899 --> 00:04:23.200
Hi there. I'm Ash.

77
00:04:23.266 --> 00:04:26.033
And these are my partners, Pikachu and Frogadier.

78
00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.133
- Pikachu.
- Frogadier.

79
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.200
Nice to meet you. I'm Serena.

80
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.633
My name's Bonnie.

81
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.166
This is Dedenne, and this is Squishy.

82
00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:36.066
I get to look after both of them.

83
00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.333
Denne.

84
00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.100
I'm Bonnie's brother, Clemont.

85
00:04:39.166 --> 00:04:40.366
It's nice to meet you.

86
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:42.300
It's nice to meet all of you.

87
00:04:42.366 --> 00:04:44.633
I'm Ippei, Sanpei's oldest brother.

88
00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.766
Yes. And I'm his other brother, Nihei.

89
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:49.000
- Hi.
- Pika, pika.

90
00:04:49.066 --> 00:04:52.000
Friends of Sanpei are friends of ours, too.

91
00:04:52.066 --> 00:04:54.900
My name's Hanzo, and I bid you all welcome.

92
00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.333
Greetings, chief. I've just gotten back home.

93
00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.433
Ja.

94
00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.500
Welcome back.

95
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:04.133
Saizo has told me just how hard you two have been training.

96
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.233
Really?

97
00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.033
Indeed. And about your friends.

98
00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.600
Really? He did that?

99
00:05:18.066 --> 00:05:20.166
Hey, Clemont, what does "chief" mean?

100
00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:21.433
It means "leader."

101
00:05:21.666 --> 00:05:23.033
He's the head ninja?

102
00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.333
That's awesome.

103
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.133
Oh, now, now, come on. You're embarrassing me.

104
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.766
Oh, chief. Are you all right?

105
00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:34.966
Please, relax.

106
00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.866
I'm fine. You're sweet to be concerned, Shinobu.

107
00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.000
Perhaps I've caught a cold.

108
00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:42.333
Oops.

109
00:05:43.533 --> 00:05:45.033
It's a ninja body switch.

110
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.800
Amazing.

111
00:05:46.866 --> 00:05:47.800
Denne.

112
00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:50.566
My name is Shinobu, and I'm the chief's assistant.

113
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.766
Nice to meet you.

114
00:05:52.233 --> 00:05:54.766
You're a keeper. Yay, Shinobu.

115
00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.033
Will you please take care of my brother?

116
00:05:58.133 --> 00:05:59.433
Den-en-enne.

117
00:06:00.366 --> 00:06:03.066
Nobody could take better care of Clemont than you.

118
00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:05.200
- You'd make me so happy.
- Ha-ha-ha.

119
00:06:05.266 --> 00:06:06.833
Please, Bonnie, stop.

120
00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.333
Come on.

121
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.366
Thank you.

122
00:06:09.433 --> 00:06:11.333
I realize that I look very young.

123
00:06:12.366 --> 00:06:16.266
So, people simply assume that I'm young, but...

124
00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.033
Shinobu is actually 100 years old.

125
00:06:20.366 --> 00:06:22.100
Why don't we just forget about it?

126
00:06:22.666 --> 00:06:25.066
You're so sweet. Honest, too.

127
00:06:26.233 --> 00:06:28.100
Lady ninja are amazing.

128
00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:31.300
It would be great if you would show us all how you've grown, Sanpei.

129
00:06:31.633 --> 00:06:33.800
And you can do that by having a battle with me.

130
00:06:33.866 --> 00:06:34.700
Yeah.

131
00:06:43.766 --> 00:06:47.100
Nihei's the second-strongest ninja in the village, right, Clemont?

132
00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.433
I heard his strength is only second to his brother Ippei.

133
00:06:51.866 --> 00:06:53.300
Let's do it, Venusaur.

134
00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.333
Saur.

135
00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.533
A Venusaur.

136
00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.333
Huh?

137
00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.866
Venusaur. The Seed Pokémon.

138
00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.000
When Venusaur spreads out its large flower petals

139
00:07:05.066 --> 00:07:07.866
and absorbs the rays of the sun, it becomes energized.

140
00:07:08.333 --> 00:07:10.366
Oh, I wonder how it battles.

141
00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.866
All right, Sanpei. I won't go easy on you.

142
00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.566
I hope you wouldn't.

143
00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.600
Okay, Greninja, use Double Team.

144
00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:23.800
Use Vine Whip.

145
00:07:23.866 --> 00:07:24.900
Aim for the legs.

146
00:07:29.966 --> 00:07:31.466
Venusaur, use Razor Leaf.

147
00:07:31.533 --> 00:07:33.433
Venusaur!

148
00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:35.466
Greninja, Water Shuriken.

149
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.433
Greninja, use Night Slash.

150
00:07:46.566 --> 00:07:47.666
Venusaur.

151
00:07:48.533 --> 00:07:49.433
Great job.

152
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.600
- Nice work, Greninja.
- Pika!

153
00:07:51.666 --> 00:07:55.400
I see Greninja's speed and power are on a whole different level now.

154
00:07:55.466 --> 00:07:57.166
You've become strong, Greninja.

155
00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:02.000
Ah.

156
00:08:02.433 --> 00:08:03.833
Let's stay on offense.

157
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.300
Greninja, use Night Slash.

158
00:08:06.366 --> 00:08:08.566
Conceal yourself with Petal Blizzard now.

159
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.000
All right. Use Razor Leaf now.

160
00:08:24.866 --> 00:08:26.733
You've got to get up, Greninja.

161
00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.100
Greninja.

162
00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:30.866
Venusaur, Solar Beam.

163
00:08:31.333 --> 00:08:34.066
Venusaur!

164
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.900
Greninja!
That's it.

165
00:08:44.466 --> 00:08:45.700
Greninja, be strong.

166
00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:46.800
Hang in there.

167
00:08:47.033 --> 00:08:49.033
- Pikachu.
- Frog-og-adier.

168
00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.266
I didn't stand a chance against him.

169
00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.533
- Not a chance.
- Indeed.

170
00:08:56.266 --> 00:08:58.466
You left far too many openings to beat him.

171
00:08:58.533 --> 00:09:01.900
Against anyone else, you should have been able to claim victory

172
00:09:01.966 --> 00:09:03.866
with your very first Night Slash.

173
00:09:06.433 --> 00:09:08.100
Chief? I guess I don't understand.

174
00:09:08.566 --> 00:09:09.933
You must not have noticed.

175
00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.633
Venusaur skillfully blocked your Night Slash

176
00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.600
mere moments before it made contact.

177
00:09:18.333 --> 00:09:19.633
It blocked it that fast?

178
00:09:20.433 --> 00:09:22.166
We took the least amount of damage...

179
00:09:22.466 --> 00:09:24.633
and waited for an opportunity to counterattack.

180
00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.800
Guess I should expect that from the number two ninja.

181
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.566
That said, you still battled well against Venusaur,

182
00:09:31.633 --> 00:09:34.100
who has a type advantage over Greninja.

183
00:09:34.266 --> 00:09:36.633
Quite commendable. You've grown.

184
00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:37.866
Thank you.

185
00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:41.566
It's easy to see that you've trained very hard with Greninja.

186
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.866
And I hope that you'll keep up the good work.

187
00:09:44.333 --> 00:09:45.900
- Right.
- Gren.

188
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:55.866
Huh? Who would have thought ninja boy's home would be in that place?

189
00:09:56.333 --> 00:09:58.000
Greninja and Venusaur, eh?

190
00:09:58.066 --> 00:10:00.866
I'll bet there are more skilled Pokémon in residence, too.

191
00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:03.133
And if we get our paws on that bunch,

192
00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.233
we can form a Team Rocket nifty ninja squad. Yeah!

193
00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.133
Creative.

194
00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.433
Strengthening ourselves with ninja power.

195
00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.533
Conquering Kalos will be like a walk in the ninja park.

196
00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.400
Catching them all is where it's at.

197
00:10:14.466 --> 00:10:16.400
Creativity's my middle name.

198
00:10:16.533 --> 00:10:18.333
We'll go and show our strength

199
00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.600
to the citizens of Ninja Village, won't we?

200
00:10:20.666 --> 00:10:22.066
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

201
00:10:22.566 --> 00:10:23.900
Wobbuffet!

202
00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:35.733
- Let us begin.
- Sir.

203
00:10:40.966 --> 00:10:42.833
Who's that Pokémon?

204
00:10:47.966 --> 00:10:50.066
It's Venusaur.

205
00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.433
Venusaur.

206
00:11:02.533 --> 00:11:04.333
This is like a secret base.

207
00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.733
It's so exciting.

208
00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:09.500
So, you have these natural caves for your homes.

209
00:11:09.566 --> 00:11:12.366
They sure look like really comfortable places to live.

210
00:11:12.433 --> 00:11:13.300
Pikachu.

211
00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:15.666
Here. Welcome to my room.

212
00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.066
Please, come right on in.

213
00:11:19.233 --> 00:11:21.266
Wow, it's really normal in here.

214
00:11:23.666 --> 00:11:26.733
- Ah. There's nothing like being home.
- Ja.

215
00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.000
Froga?

216
00:11:29.666 --> 00:11:32.666
Hmm? Look at that. It's a Froakie.

217
00:11:33.766 --> 00:11:35.400
You took this before you left?

218
00:11:35.866 --> 00:11:38.266
Yes. To remember things as they were then.

219
00:11:39.033 --> 00:11:42.666
My goal is to become the best Pokémon trainer in the village.

220
00:11:43.133 --> 00:11:45.600
But I couldn't defeat my brother Nihei.

221
00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.866
It's clear I won't stand a chance against Ippei, either.

222
00:11:49.466 --> 00:11:51.300
I still need to train a lot more.

223
00:11:52.133 --> 00:11:54.466
So, what are your plans now, Sanpei?

224
00:11:55.566 --> 00:11:57.766
I'm going to stay here and train hard.

225
00:11:58.766 --> 00:12:00.633
And help my brothers out, as well.

226
00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.966
Help them how?

227
00:12:02.266 --> 00:12:05.866
Well, it's been decided that Ippei will become the next chief.

228
00:12:05.933 --> 00:12:07.000
The chief?

229
00:12:07.433 --> 00:12:11.300
Yes. Hanzo is going to retire, after tomorrow's village festival.

230
00:12:11.966 --> 00:12:15.066
From now on my brothers and I will be combining forces

231
00:12:15.133 --> 00:12:16.800
in order to protect Ninja Village.

232
00:12:17.266 --> 00:12:19.600
Awesome. I know the three of you will be great.

233
00:12:19.666 --> 00:12:20.500
Pika, pika.

234
00:12:20.566 --> 00:12:22.166
- Thanks.
- Frogadier.

235
00:12:22.233 --> 00:12:23.066
Grenin.

236
00:12:23.133 --> 00:12:25.500
Pikachu, we need to keep getting stronger, too.

237
00:12:25.566 --> 00:12:26.733
Pikachu.

238
00:12:37.833 --> 00:12:40.433
Huh? Dedenne?

239
00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:42.733
Squishy?

240
00:12:43.533 --> 00:12:44.566
That's weird.

241
00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.700
Uh, Dedenne?

242
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:47.833
Squishy?

243
00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.000
What's wrong, Bonnie?

244
00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.566
Do you think...?

245
00:12:54.566 --> 00:12:55.700
A trap door.

246
00:12:56.366 --> 00:12:59.766
It's possible they went through here, and got into the secret passageway.

247
00:13:00.066 --> 00:13:01.366
I've gotta find them.

248
00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.766
Wait. It's too dangerous.

249
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.100
Sanpei, what's down there, anyway?

250
00:13:10.333 --> 00:13:11.600
Let's go down, too.

251
00:13:29.766 --> 00:13:30.600
Gotcha.

252
00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.533
I thought they'd be here.

253
00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.600
I'm so glad we found you.

254
00:13:42.666 --> 00:13:44.400
Oh, so, they came from your room, then.

255
00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.233
I was so worried.

256
00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.000
Excuse me. That's my line.

257
00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:55.433
What an amazing place.

258
00:13:57.233 --> 00:13:59.433
And it's all inside a cave.

259
00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.466
This is a monument dedicated to the hero of the village.

260
00:14:02.566 --> 00:14:04.066
- Hero?
- Yes.

261
00:14:04.366 --> 00:14:05.400
Let me show you.

262
00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:19.400
Look at that.

263
00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.900
Wow. I think that's a Pokémon.

264
00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.366
Does that mean the village hero is a Pokémon, then?

265
00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:30.766
Yes. There's a legend that states a fierce battle broke out

266
00:14:30.833 --> 00:14:32.700
between all the ninja in our village.

267
00:14:33.033 --> 00:14:35.766
Yeah? The ninja were fighting other ninja?

268
00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:37.133
Why were they fighting?

269
00:14:37.266 --> 00:14:40.333
Well, there's no way to find out what caused it now,

270
00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.066
but we do know the ones who defended the village back then were Pokémon.

271
00:14:44.933 --> 00:14:47.933
And this Greninja was the leader of those Pokémon.

272
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.033
Honestly?

273
00:14:50.366 --> 00:14:53.966
I chose Froakie as my partner because I admired the village hero.

274
00:14:54.033 --> 00:14:56.600
I raised Froakie, who evolved into Frogadier,

275
00:14:56.666 --> 00:14:57.900
and then into Greninja.

276
00:14:59.166 --> 00:15:02.166
- Yeah. It's the same story for me, too.
- Gren.

277
00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.833
But that Greninja looks different than ones I've seen before.

278
00:15:06.633 --> 00:15:07.633
Huh?

279
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.600
Maybe you're right.

280
00:15:19.733 --> 00:15:22.200
You're really making that sparkle.

281
00:15:26.466 --> 00:15:29.666
Yes. But in the end, this is merely an accessory.

282
00:15:29.933 --> 00:15:33.733
What really matters is having the trust of all our villagers.

283
00:15:34.066 --> 00:15:36.333
I'm certain Ippei will be fine.

284
00:15:37.433 --> 00:15:38.566
Oh, my.

285
00:15:38.966 --> 00:15:42.633
No one makes tea as delicious as you do, dear Shinobu.

286
00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.466
Thank you so much, Hanzo.

287
00:15:50.166 --> 00:15:54.466
To review, we're going to create a ruckus, and then gather the Pokémon in the square.

288
00:15:54.533 --> 00:15:58.733
Which is when we catch them all, executing our plan with sheer perfection.

289
00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.466
And it's all in the bucket.

290
00:16:00.833 --> 00:16:02.033
Wob-buf!

291
00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.966
Wait. We've got company up here?

292
00:16:27.333 --> 00:16:28.333
Skarmory?

293
00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:31.900
What's going on?!

294
00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.533
- What's that?
- Oh, no.

295
00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:41.866
It's the outside alarm.

296
00:16:41.933 --> 00:16:42.933
Listen, Sanpei.

297
00:16:43.133 --> 00:16:45.400
You take your friends over to Hanzo's place,

298
00:16:45.466 --> 00:16:46.633
and we'll go have a look.

299
00:16:46.866 --> 00:16:47.900
Right, Ippei.

300
00:16:47.966 --> 00:16:49.066
- Come on.
- All right.

301
00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.000
Venusaur!

302
00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.066
- Nihei.
- Hey.

303
00:17:19.133 --> 00:17:20.066
Is anybody hurt?

304
00:17:20.133 --> 00:17:21.666
No, I think everyone's all right.

305
00:17:23.033 --> 00:17:25.433
Ippei, please, can you tell us what's going on here?

306
00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.366
They're well-trained, for sure.

307
00:17:32.733 --> 00:17:34.166
Definitely not wild.

308
00:17:34.533 --> 00:17:35.366
But why?

309
00:17:35.433 --> 00:17:38.433
Why? Who knows? They started attacking out of nowhere.

310
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.666
Aah! They're back.

311
00:17:42.733 --> 00:17:44.200
Greninja, let's go.

312
00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.433
Chief, it's me.

313
00:17:47.733 --> 00:17:49.566
Oh, Sanpei and your friends.

314
00:17:49.633 --> 00:17:51.966
My brothers told us to come to your place and wait.

315
00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:14.966
Who are you?

316
00:18:15.166 --> 00:18:16.700
State your names now.

317
00:18:17.166 --> 00:18:22.066
Now then, Hanzo, chief of Ninja Village, you'll be coming with us.

318
00:18:37.333 --> 00:18:39.400
- Oh, no, Hanzo.
- Pika!

319
00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:42.600
You bring Hanzo back.

320
00:18:42.666 --> 00:18:44.666
Release our chief right away.

321
00:18:46.133 --> 00:18:47.300
Pika, pi.

322
00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:49.000
Ash, no!

323
00:18:50.966 --> 00:18:51.800
You can't go.

324
00:18:52.266 --> 00:18:54.333
- But what about Ash?
- It's too dangerous.

325
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.933
We need to find Ippei.

326
00:18:56.733 --> 00:18:58.600
- Ippei?
- Don't worry. Come on.

327
00:19:01.266 --> 00:19:02.266
But Ash.

328
00:19:03.066 --> 00:19:04.066
Greninja.

329
00:19:04.633 --> 00:19:06.500
Use Water Shuriken now.

330
00:19:09.233 --> 00:19:11.700
All right, Venusaur, now use Razor Leaf.

331
00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.300
Venusaur.

332
00:19:15.266 --> 00:19:17.100
Simisage, Bullet Seed.

333
00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.233
Simipour, use Ice Beam.

334
00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.166
It's the end of the line.

335
00:19:38.633 --> 00:19:41.100
Our ruckus is already created.

336
00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:43.233
Oh, what's the difference?

337
00:19:43.433 --> 00:19:45.233
It'll still get the job done.

338
00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.066
Any kind of chaos is still chaos, right?

339
00:19:48.166 --> 00:19:49.566
Wobbuffet!

340
00:19:49.633 --> 00:19:53.633
Simipour, Simisage, Greninja, and Venusaur.

341
00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.800
Conveniently located for quick catching.

342
00:19:56.566 --> 00:19:58.666
So, the sooner we catch them, the better.

343
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.800
Ippei. The chief.

344
00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.133
Look out.

345
00:20:05.333 --> 00:20:06.200
Behind you.

346
00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:13.600
- Team Rocket.
- Team Rocket.

347
00:20:16.133 --> 00:20:16.966
Bisharp!

348
00:20:22.966 --> 00:20:24.833
The normally peaceful Ninja Village

349
00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:28.433
is suddenly under a fierce attack by mysterious forces.

350
00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.066
What can they be after?

351
00:20:32.266 --> 00:20:34.633
And what will become of Chief Hanzo?

352
00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:40.233
The answers to come, as our heroes' journey continues.
